  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ramanagouda vs The State Of Karnataka on 11 December, 2018 Author: John Michael Cunha Bench: John Michael Cunha 1 In The High Court Of Karnataka Kalaburagi Bench Dated This The 11Th Day Of December, 2018 Before The Hon'Ble Mr. Justice John Michael Cunha Criminal Petition No.201319/2017 Between : Ramanagouda S/O Hanumanagouda Age: 61 Years, Occ: Agriculturist R/O Muddamguddi Village, Manvi Taluka Dist: Raichur-585401 ... Petitioner (By Sri Mahantesh Patil, Advocate) And: The State Of Karnataka Represented By Spp High Court Of Karnataka Kalaburagi Bench-585107 (Through Manvi Ps) ... Respondent",
    "facts": "2. Petitioner has sought to quash the order dated 19.06.2013 whereby the JMFC Manvi has taken cognizance of the offence under section 3(1)(ZZ)(VII), 42 (4)(A) and 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. 3. The brief facts of the case are as follows: On the basis of the information furnished by Raitha Sangharsha Hasiru Nisane, Manvi, the Tahsildar, Manvi Taluk conducted a raid on the godown of M/s Channabasaveshwar Trading Company, Potanal Village and seized 520 bags of jowar and 10 bags of sodium meta bi sulphate powder. Based on the report submitted by the Tahsildar, SHO of Manvi Police Station registered a case against the petitioner in Crime No.180/2012 under Section 3(1)(ZZ)(VII), 42 (4)(A) and 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. On completing the investigation, charge sheet was laid before the learned Magistrate. The learned Magistrate by the impugned order has taken cognizance of the above offences and issued summons to the petitioner.",
    "arguments": "The contention of the petitioner is that very initiation of the criminal action against him is illegal and contrary to the provisions of the Food Safety and Standard Act. 4. In terms of Section 41 of the said Act, powers of search, seizure and investigation are vested with the Food Safety Officer. As per Section 42 of the said Act, the Food Safety Officer is the only competent authority to launch prosecution for the violation of the provisions of the Act. In view of the above provisions of law, raid conducted by the Tahsildar as well as the consequent registration of the FIR and the investigation are bad in law and amount to abuse of the process of the court. 5. Learned High Court Government Pleader does not dispute the fact, that the Tahsildar has no jurisdiction to take action in the alleged violation of the provisions of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The contention of the petitioner is that very initiation of the criminal action against him is illegal and contrary to the provisions of the Food Safety and Standard Act. 4. In terms of Section 41 of the said Act, powers of search, seizure and investigation are vested with the Food Safety Officer. As per Section 42 of the said Act, the Food Safety Officer is the only competent authority to launch prosecution for the violation of the provisions of the Act. In view of the above provisions of law, raid conducted by the Tahsildar as well as the consequent registration of the FIR and the investigation are bad in law and amount to abuse of the process of the court. 5. Learned High Court Government Pleader does not dispute the fact, that the Tahsildar has no jurisdiction to take action in the alleged violation of the provisions of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006.",
